def fmt(r,n):return f'{r:,}/{n:,} ({100*r/n:.2f}%)'if n else'N/A'
lines=['# BundleGraph v2: structural multi-bundler relationship analysis','','Date: 2026-10-23. This is a new implementation/experiment; frozen baselines and prior v1 results remain unchanged. Models invoked: **0**.','','The new tool uses bundler runtime mechanisms to normalize module registrations, loaders and exports into a shared bounded pointer/value analysis. Its generic CLI accepts a build artifact manifest, independently of repository/library names or ground truth. Source maps and frozen correspondences enter only the separate experiment evaluation.','','## Implemented architecture','','1. Collect relative dependency context within supplied roots, including runtime-only files. Keep the target population separate. Record missing/computed/external dependencies; do not guess dynamic filenames.','2. Normalize lexical bindings, constant string expressions, table shapes, factory aliases and global addresses. Lexical aliases and global registry paths use bounded worklists, avoiding recursive alias-tree expansion.','3. Map runtime mechanisms to common module/exports/require or context operations. Webpack-compatible bootstrap, sparse legacy tables, custom/pushed registries and exported tables share module records; Rolldown, Turbopack and Parcel use dedicated calling-convention adapters. Flattened/ESM code uses lexical import/export edges.','4. Resolve static values, getter returns and small ordinary parameter/member return summaries with a shared indexed worklist. Keep native alternatives, ambiguity and overflow abstention.','5. Export module and function relationship graphs. The existing paired-neighborhood simulation remains separate, with no module-membership cliques or initialization-function matching.','','[Implementation and CLI](../../../scripts/real-app/bundle-graph-v2/README.md), [design](../../../scripts/real-app/bundle-graph-v2/DESIGN.md). The source copies under `code/` are the exact local implementation; execute the workspace paths shown there.','','The analyzer organization follows the runtime-map and wrapper-parameter approach discussed in [D-Bundlr §3.2](https://reallytg.github.io/files/papers/debundling_icse.pdf). This is not reproduction of its predictor, sandbox, rewriting or CodeQL pipeline.','','## Validation','','- 28 focused unit/regression tests pass, including sparse/bootstrap tables, registry aliases, environment partitioning, getter helper contracts, native-polyfill abstention, bounded alias diamonds and context collection.','- All 37 fully supplied mutation probes pass. The 38th deliberately removes the helper input and remains unresolved; the separate filesystem-closure test supplies that helper automatically when it exists. This is deliberate context abstention, not a passing relationship probe.','- 16 actual local webpack 5.97.1 builds: eight configurations, each with a base and edited application. Checked entry calls resolve in all 16; the checked internal lazy-module call resolves in all 14 splitting cases. Two flattened ESM cases retain no module wrappers and use lexical relationships. This is a tiny deterministic matrix, not held-out large applications or a webpack-version-wide accuracy claim.','- 12 actual esbuild 0.25.9 / Rollup 4.50.0 builds: ESM, CommonJS and IIFE, each with a base/edited application. Both retained intended calls resolve in all 12.','- Module tables recognized in 17 pinned real webpack 1/3/4/5-era chunks. Counts match the original D-Bundlr recognizer on all 11 webpack 1/3 chunks. Counts on later chunks include nested tables and are not a boundary-precision oracle. The original comparator is not run on the later chunks after it stalled in development.','- Twelve fresh-process synthetic scale cases cover 500/2,000/8,000 modules per family; all generated expected direct calls resolve. One trial per case; simple chains do not establish asymptotic or ecosystem-wide scalability.','','| Family | 8,000 modules: seconds | Completion RSS MiB | Expected / found direct calls |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
for r in scale:
 if r['modules']==8000:lines.append(f"| {r['family']} | {r['elapsedMs']/1000:.3f} | {r['rssEndMiB']} | {r['expectedCallEdges']} / {r['observedCallEdges']} |")
lines+=['','The module-graph exporter now indexes lazy records by key rather than scanning all modules per lazy require. Runtime aliases and registry addresses have independent bounded worklists as well as the value solver. Completion RSS is not sampled peak memory. Whole-build constraint state is retained; only AST retention is limited to one compiled unit.','','## Frozen-target connectivity comparison','','Eight non-esbuild subjects, 69 repo/library cases, 62 with supported pairs. Denominators count source/bundle function pairs per prepared chunk, not unique source functions. The oracle, targets, initial POG seeds, sibling window two, radius one, 18,000-character limit and same-chunk uniqueness policy remain fixed. Context-only chunks have no new matchable function IDs. Cross-chunk results remain separate.','','| Repository | Targets | Frozen baseline | V1 per chunk | V2 per chunk | V1 cross-chunk | V2 cross-chunk |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for r in repo_rows:lines.append('| '+r['repo']+' | '+str(r['targets'])+' | '+' | '.join(fmt(r[k],r['targets'])for k in ['baseline','v1-per-chunk','v2-per-chunk','v1-cross-chunk','v2-cross-chunk'])+' |')
lines.append('| **Total** | '+f"{totals['targets']:,}"+' | '+' | '.join(fmt(totals[k],totals['targets'])for k in ['baseline','v1-per-chunk','v2-per-chunk','v1-cross-chunk','v2-cross-chunk'])+' |')
lines+=['','V2 retains the full frozen baseline recovered-pair sets and has no per-library count regressions against v1. The evaluator checks exact target/seed hashes, paired promotion witnesses and independent BFS reachability. These are oracle connectivity results, not measured model recovery, whole-library recall, or independent edge precision.','','The ZyPlayer icon library now reaches 41,489/41,489 pairs in the automatic run, using four unchanged icon seeds. Its missing runtime helper is collected as context. All ten sampled native-polyfill edges rejected during v1 auditing remain absent; the gain does not reinstate those edges.','','## Analysis-context and scale records','','| Repository | Prepared + context units | Context-only units | Source / bundle seconds | Source / bundle completion RSS MiB |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for c in contexts:lines.append(f"| {c['repo']} | {c['units']} | {c['contextOnlyUnits']} | {c['sourceMs']/1000:.2f} / {c['bundleMs']/1000:.2f} | {c['sourceRSSMiB']} / {c['bundleRSSMiB']} |")
lines+=['','Context diagnostics are retained per subject in `bundle-relations.json`: a supplied closure can still have external/bare or computed requests. They are not silently treated as resolved. Saved non-target artifacts are context, and their semantic effects can change ambiguity; targets/seeds remain fixed. `context-inputs/` captures exact code by hash for later replay.','','## Remaining scope','','The tool supports the tested protocol families and provides reusable adapters; the evidence does not establish a success percentage for most repositories. Development/HMR, module federation, arbitrary plugin wrappers, property-mangled runtimes, full async/bound-function/Promise flow, general higher-order flow and computed chunk URL evaluation remain unvalidated or partial. Independent runtime groups need explicit input partitioning. The frozen experiment keeps its existing worker/target population; it is not a new audit of every runtime realm.','','Scope-hoisting can erase original module boundaries; lexical relationships are recovered without inventing those boundaries. Source TS/TSX parse failures and unpaired transformations are unchanged in the frozen denominator. Native opaque alternatives and a singleton modeled target policy help avoid known over-approximations, but the tool is not a sound full-JavaScript analyzer and high connectivity cannot establish precision. A larger held-out rebuild corpus is still needed before an ecosystem-wide claim.','','## Files','','- `per-library.csv`: every library, fixed denominator and baseline/v1/v2 counts.','- `per-repo.csv`, `aggregate.json`, `verification.json`: aggregate metrics and validation ledger.','- `subjects/<slug>/*-relations.json`: code-only relationships, module graph, context/coverage diagnostics and provenance.','- `subjects/<slug>/target-traces.json`: evaluation-only rounds, final gates and paired witnesses.','- `context-inputs/<sha256>.js`: exact captured context; `replay.mjs` can replay bundle extraction using it and the immutable inventory.','- `validation/`: probe inputs/results, real legacy chunk counts, test output, scale results.','- `webpack-matrix/`, `esm-matrix/`: generated source edits, real build output and analyzed graphs.','- `code/`: exact implementation, CLI usage and design.','','Primary mechanism references: [webpack output](https://webpack.js.org/configuration/output/), [Rspack output](https://rspack.rs/config/output), [Rolldown runtime](https://github.com/rolldown/rolldown/blob/main/crates/rolldown/src/runtime/runtime-base.js), [Turbopack runtime](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/blob/v16.2.6/turbopack/crates/turbopack-ecmascript-runtime/js/src/shared/runtime/runtime-utils.ts), [Parcel helpers](https://github.com/parcel-bundler/parcel/blob/v2/packages/packagers/js/src/helpers.js). Actual measured formats are pinned by the corpus/build artifacts, not by assuming current upstream is identical.','']
(OUT/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines));snapshot=OUT/'code';snapshot.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
